WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.960
Zazie Beetz is far from a household name,
but her role in the upcoming Deadpool sequel

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.150
just might change all that.

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:10.280
In the scant five years that Beetz''s IMDb
profile has been active, she's racked up a

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.809
respectable number of credits.

00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:15.900
Here's why Domino from Deadpool 2 looks so
familiar.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.220
Wolves

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:21.689
Zazie started her career like most other up-and-coming
actors in their mid-20s - by playing high

00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:23.020
school students.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.869
Wolves is the age-old urban tale of a young
man named Anthony, who uses his prowess on

00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:31.369
the basketball court to escape a far more
complicated home life.

00:00:31.369 --> 00:00:36.070
Beetz is Victoria, Lee's love interest, whose
arc revolves around her desperate desire to

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:38.360
know all the parts of him that he keeps hidden.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:42.809
Shot during the summer of 2015, Wolves is
the project that let Beetz give up her day

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.770
job and pursue acting full time.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.949
The film took a one-way ticket to Highbrow
Town by premiering at the Tribeca Film Festival

00:00:48.949 --> 00:00:52.149
before being picked up for distribution by
IFC Films.

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:55.039
​Margot vs. Lily

00:00:55.039 --> 00:00:59.079
In 2016, Nike decided that a cute, diverse,
and surprisingly well-made web series was

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:03.679
the best way to promote their workout clothes,
and Margot vs. Lily was the result.

00:01:03.679 --> 00:01:08.100
As part of the "Better For It" Women's campaign,
this was Nike's first scripted show, and it

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.950
got a nice amount of positive buzz in part
because the commercial elements were integrated

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:13.640
well into the narrative.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.300
"Allie!

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.140
I think I might be jacked!

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:20.460
Arms so sore, arms like Thor…"

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:21.479
"Wow!

00:01:21.479 --> 00:01:24.090
I've never seen you like this in the morning."

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:28.380
Beetz plays Allie, best friend and roommate
to Margot, a snarky millennial with a chip

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.390
on her shoulder who lives and plots in the
shadow of her internet-famous fitness guru

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:34.620
sister Lily.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:35.770
Easy

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:39.990
This Netflix Original lacks the buzz or prestige
of some of their other high profile shows

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:44.170
like Stranger Things or House of Cards, but
Easy does have that rambling indie quality

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.340
that seems to fit nicely within Beetz's filmography.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:51.729
This sexy ensemble drama follows a chain of
interlinking friends navigating the ups and

00:01:51.729 --> 00:01:56.049
downs of their intimate relationships; Beetz
plays Noell, a sweet and supportive stoner

00:01:56.049 --> 00:02:00.450
who's dating an amateur brewer named Jeff
- played by Dave Franco - who has ambitions

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.780
of starting an illegal brewery with his more
conservative brother.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:07.450
"Imagine you were pregnant and I didn't tell
you about any of this.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.970
What would you do What would you do?"

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:10.560
"I would freak out!"

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:11.120
"Exactly!"

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:13.640
Atlanta

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:18.090
Much ink has been spilled about the groundbreaking
Atlanta, Donald Glover's Emmy-winning MC Escher

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.820
painting of an urban drama.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:24.440
Beetz plays Van, a young mother in love with
Glover's Earn, the father of her daughter,

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:29.880
who at turns she's completely enamored with
and totally frustrated by due to his underachieving,

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.390
spacey, charismatic brilliance.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:35.290
"Uh, you're doing that weird sad boy face
you've got sometimes."

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:36.710
"That's just my face."

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:40.770
This role is tailor made to make use of all
that Beetz has to offer as an actor, and is

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:45.940
likely the reason she was on the Deadpool
creative team's radar to begin with.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:47.100
Geostorm

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:52.370
Even though her role is small, 2017's Geostorm
marks Beetz's first appearance in a high-profile

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:53.370
film.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:57.490
She plays Dana, a cybersecurity analyst and
friend to Max, played by Jim Sturgess.

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:02.240
The disaster flick was unfortunately reamed
by critics, but Beetz was still able to inject

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.150
some expositional technobabble and moments
of levity opposite Sturgess — and when she

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:11.570
appears in Deadpool 2, it won't be her first
time at the blockbuster rodeo.

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:12.730
The Boss

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:17.760
If you can make it through this squirmy January
2018 dramatization of a real-life workplace

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:22.780
harassment, you'll see Beetz go from an efficient
and helpful professional to confused, then

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:27.210
alarmed, then panicked as her boss proceeds
to violate her space completely.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:31.720
This wasn't just another acting job — it's
a PSA executive produced by Beetz' co-star

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:32.920
David Schwimmer.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:37.170
It's among a series of short films released
online designed to raise awareness about RAINN,

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:41.160
the nation's largest anti-sexual violence
organization.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.910
Deadpool 2

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:47.230
Months before anyone got to see her in action
as Domino, Beetz was part of the vast media

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:49.210
machine surrounding the Deadpool sequel.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:53.340
Her casting was announced via Ryan Reynolds's
Twitter with a character poster, and her arrival

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.310
quickly generated a ton of buzz.

00:03:55.310 --> 00:04:01.010
In the world of comics, Domino, a.k.a. Neena
Thurman, debuted in the pages of X-Force #8

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:02.160
in 1992.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:06.310
Her power to affect the probability of any
event within her line of sight is the result

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.650
of a government experiment.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:12.370
She's joined various mercenary bands and also
rolled solo throughout her history.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:17.060
Beetz may seem an odd choice to play the pistol-packing,
motorcycle-revving mercenary mutant — but

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.560
her fresh take might be just what the role
needs.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.660
Thanks for watching!

